@baseAddress = http://localhost:5000

### Get AgentCard for weather agent (agent discovery)
GET {{baseAddress}}/a2a/weather/card

### Ask the weather agent (streaming SSE response)
# Each request needs a unique messageId — Message.MessageId is [JsonRequired].
# {{$guid}} is a VS Code REST Client variable; replace with any unique string
# if your HTTP client doesn't support it.
# contextId maintains conversation history — reuse the same ID for follow-up questions.
POST {{baseAddress}}/a2a/weather/message:stream
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": {
    "role": "user",
    "parts": [
      { "text": "What is the weather like in Amsterdam this time of year?" }
    ],
    "messageId": "{{$guid}}",
    "contextId": "weather-conversation-1"
  }
}

### Follow-up in the same conversation (reuses contextId, new messageId)
POST {{baseAddress}}/a2a/weather/message:stream
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": {
    "role": "user",
    "parts": [
      { "text": "What about in December — should I pack a heavy coat?" }
    ],
    "messageId": "{{$guid}}",
    "contextId": "weather-conversation-1"
  }
}

### Ask the travel agent (non-streaming JSON response)
POST {{baseAddress}}/a2a/travel/message:send
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": {
    "role": "user",
    "parts": [
      { "text": "I want to visit Amsterdam for 3 days. What are the must-see sights?" }
    ],
    "messageId": "{{$guid}}",
    "contextId": "travel-conversation-1"
  }
}

### Use the sequential workflow (weather agent → travel agent)
POST {{baseAddress}}/a2a/trip-planning/message:send
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": {
    "role": "user",
    "parts": [
      { "text": "Help me plan a trip to Amsterdam in October." }
    ],
    "messageId": "{{$guid}}",
    "contextId": "planning-conversation-1"
  }
}
